1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,072
Everyone climbs Sigiriya.

2
00:00:02,072 --> 00:00:03,768
Few hear its secrets.

3
00:00:04,468 --> 00:00:06,738
1,500 years ago, Prince Kashyapa

4
00:00:06,738 --> 00:00:09,053
seized his father's throne.

5
00:00:09,053 --> 00:00:10,743
The chronicle says he

6
00:00:10,743 --> 00:00:12,916
walled his father up alive.

7
00:00:12,916 --> 00:00:14,445
His brother fled to

8
00:00:14,445 --> 00:00:16,144
India for an army.

9
00:00:16,894 --> 00:00:19,426
So he built his capital

10
00:00:19,426 --> 00:00:22,538
on a rock 180 metres high.

11
00:00:23,588 --> 00:00:25,351
Secret one: climbers once

12
00:00:25,351 --> 00:00:27,706
walked into a lion's mouth.

13
00:00:27,706 --> 00:00:29,083
A giant brick lion

14
00:00:29,083 --> 00:00:30,996
guarded the final stairs.

15
00:00:30,996 --> 00:00:32,930
Only its paws survive.

16
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:35,338
Secret two: the

17
00:00:35,338 --> 00:00:37,014
cliff was a gallery.

18
00:00:37,014 --> 00:00:39,865
Verses speak of 500 painted women.

19
00:00:39,865 --> 00:00:41,456
About 20 remain.

20
00:00:42,606 --> 00:00:44,126
Secret three: ancient

21
00:00:44,126 --> 00:00:45,285
visitor reviews.

22
00:00:45,285 --> 00:00:46,805
Over 1,000 years ago,

23
00:00:46,805 --> 00:00:48,615
people scratched poems to

24
00:00:48,615 --> 00:00:51,310
those women on the Mirror Wall.

25
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:54,432
685 were read in 1956.

26
00:00:54,432 --> 00:00:58,513
Since then, about 800 more.

27
00:00:59,463 --> 00:01:01,345
Secret four: in the rains,

28
00:01:01,345 --> 00:01:03,154
the fountains still rise.

29
00:01:03,154 --> 00:01:04,819
Water flows from a moat

30
00:01:04,819 --> 00:01:06,700
that sits slightly higher,

31
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,832
and gravity does the rest.

32
00:01:10,182 --> 00:01:11,377
The king's end?

33
00:01:11,377 --> 00:01:14,007
His elephant turned from a swamp.

34
00:01:14,007 --> 00:01:16,557
His army thought he was fleeing,

35
00:01:16,557 --> 00:01:18,799
and he took his own life.

36
00:01:20,599 --> 00:01:22,509
But was it ever a palace?

37
00:01:22,509 --> 00:01:25,106
Archaeologist Raja de Silva argued

38
00:01:25,106 --> 00:01:27,571
it was a monastery all along.

39
00:01:28,471 --> 00:01:29,093
Sigiriya.

40
00:01:29,093 --> 00:01:31,622
The rock still keeps its secrets.
